DVB-S2X VL-SNR Modulator/Demodulator

This is an implementation of the DVB-S2X Very Low Signal-to-Noise
Ratio (VL-SNR) physical layer, covering all 9 MODCODs defined in
ETSI EN 302 307-2.  Operating range is -2 dB to -10 dB Es/N0.

Build
-----

	make
	make DEBUG=1		# debug build
	make test		# run unit tests
	make clean

Requirements: GCC with C11 support, libm.

Structure
---------

	include/	Public headers
	src/		Library source
	tables/		LDPC parity address tables
	test/		Unit tests

The build produces libdvbs2x_vlsnr.a (static library).

Signal Chain
------------

Transmitter:

	User data -> BB frame -> BCH -> LDPC -> interleave ->
	modulate (pi/2-BPSK or QPSK) -> spread (optional) ->
	PL frame (header + WH header + pilots) -> scramble ->
	RRC pulse shape -> baseband IQ

Receiver:

	Baseband IQ -> RRC matched filter -> timing recovery ->
	coarse freq (BQ-FED) -> frame sync (WH correlation) ->
	fine freq (pilot-aided) -> phase est -> descramble ->
	pilot extract -> despread (optional) -> soft demap ->
	deinterleave -> LDPC decode -> BCH decode -> BB frame
	parse -> user data

Status
------

LDPC parity address tables are placeholders.  Real values from
ETSI EN 302 307-2 Annex B must be transcribed before the LDPC
decoder will converge at operational SNR.

References
----------

ETSI EN 302 307-1 V1.4.1	DVB-S2 base standard
ETSI EN 302 307-2 V1.3.1	DVB-S2X extensions
ETSI TR 102 376-1		Implementation guidelines
ETSI TR 102 376-2		S2X implementation guidelines

